      "body": "\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\n\r\nThe kernel works on gfx950 and is a drop in replacement for fp8_mqa_logits (that's gluon), see [docstring](https://github.com/ROCm/aiter/blob/e6ded2168ef43111c57d591dd310eccdfc27aaf1/aiter/ops/flydsl/fp8_mqa_logits_kernels.py#L481).\r\n\r\n**Note**: https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/60294 and https://github.com/ROCm/aiter/pull/6185 will fix so we don't have to manually select between the gluon and flydsl mqa_logits kernel here from vllm. However those are still wip, so I suggest we move fast and delete the current manual selection once those are merged. I suspect we'd want to use flydsl in most cases anyways\r\n\r\n## Claims\r\n\r\n- 10-20% improved TTFT\r\n- 5-20% improved throughput at 64k+ ctx\r\n- Unaffected ITL (as expected) \r\n- Improvements growing with ctx len\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\n### 1. e2e sweep\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nVLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER=1 \\\r\nVLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER_TRITON_SPARSE_MLA=1 \\\r\nVLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER_FUSION_SHARED_EXPERTS=1 \\\r\nVLLM_USE_BREAKABLE_CUDAGRAPH=1 \\\r\nvllm serve zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash --tensor-parallel-size 8 --max-num-seqs 512 --gpu-memory-utilization 0.8 --attention-backend ROCM_AITER_MLA_SPARSE --max-num-batched-tokens 16384 --reasoning-parser glm47\r\n```\r\n```bash\r\n# always num_prompts=10*max_concurrency, num_warmups=2*max_concurrency\r\nvllm bench serve \\\r\n  --backend vllm --model zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash  \\\r\n  --dataset_name random --random_input_len $ISL --random_output_len 1024 \\\r\n  --max_concurrency 32 --num_prompts 320 --num_warmups 64 \\\r\n  --host localhost --port 8000 --ignore_eos --seed 56552124\r\n```\r\n\r\n| ISL | OSL | Conc | TTFT main (ms) | TTFT this branch (ms) | TTFT improv. | ITL main (ms) | ITL this branch (ms) | ITL improv. | Out tok/s main | Out tok/s this branch | Out tok/s improv. |\r\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\r\n| 512k | 1k | 4 | 22731.18 | 17497.50 | **+23.02%** | 8.85 | 8.86 | **-0.16%** | 52.58 | 64.21 | **+22.11%** |\r\n| 512k | 1k | 1 | 17088.25 | 13562.26 | **+20.63%** | 7.84 | 7.88 | **-0.45%** | 40.79 | 47.36 | **+16.12%** |\r\n| 256k | 1k | 4 | 8520.00 | 7032.57 | **+17.46%** | 8.71 | 8.67 | **+0.43%** | 118.66 | 134.23 | **+13.12%** |\r\n| 256k | 1k | 1 | 6466.89 | 5497.06 | **+15.00%** | 7.69 | 7.74 | **-0.71%** | 71.43 | 76.29 | **+6.81%** |\r\n| 64k | 1k | 8 | 1688.92 | 1508.12 | **+10.71%** | 9.58 | 9.57 | **+0.03%** | 402.44 | 424.37 | **+5.45%** |\r\n| 64k | 1k | 1 | 1324.33 | 1220.67 | **+7.83%** | 7.66 | 7.72 | **-0.71%** | 111.72 | 112.33 | **+0.55%** |\r\n| 8k | 1k | 64 | 625.06 | 578.52 | **+7.45%** | 12.71 | 12.70 | **+0.01%** | 2783.20 | 2885.86 | **+3.69%** |\r\n| 8k | 1k | 8 | 357.72 | 314.99 | **+11.94%** | 9.55 | 9.58 | **-0.32%** | 737.42 | 745.27 | **+1.06%** |\r\n| 8k | 1k | 1 | 181.00 | 158.44 | **+12.47%** | 7.66 | 7.68 | **-0.24%** | 127.70 | 127.77 | **+0.05%** |\r\n| 1k | 1k | 64 | 453.38 | 454.44 | **-0.23%** | 12.54 | 12.54 | **+0.02%** | 4487.77 | 4482.36 | **-0.12%** |\r\n| 1k | 1k | 8 | 200.64 | 207.26 | **-3.30%** | 9.43 | 9.39 | **+0.39%** | 831.57 | 834.59 | **+0.36%** |\r\n| 1k | 1k | 1 | 98.71 | 94.26 | **+4.50%** | 7.54 | 7.48 | **+0.77%** | 131.04 | 132.11 | **+0.82%** |\r\n \r\n\r\n### 2. Accuracy\r\n\r\nGPQA\r\n\r\nGSM8k\r\n\r\n### 3. Microbenchmarks\r\n\r\nSee AITER PR https://github.com/ROCm/aiter/pull/4538\r\n\r\n## Details\r\n\r\n### Before\r\n\r\nAt 512k ISL, the final chunk's indexer splits the context into **16** chunks and scores+topk's each of them individually. This happens for each of the **11** sparse MLA layers. These kernels execute in\r\n- mqa_logits: ~800us\r\n- indexer topk: 1.9ms\r\n\r\nHence we spend `800us * 11 * 16 = 140ms` on topk only, The full forward takes 800ms, so 18% of chunked prefill is spent just computing indexer logits!\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1482\" height=\"832\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4e6b3c80-9e36-4338-ac6a-47e8e7a6c3a1\" />\r\n\r\n### After\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\r\n- [ ] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\r\n\r\n- [ ] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\r\n- [ ] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\r\n- [ ] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\r\n- [ ] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n",
